  An emergency is finding a Black Dragon when you don't have reflection.
Escape and use the wish for the best source of reflection.

  Or seeing a Golden Naga when you don't have magic resistance.  Escape
and wish for the best source of MR.


  Not having an escape route in mind isn't an emergency, it's poor
preparation.


  What most people seem to consider emergencies seem like suicide.
They'll generally wait until even a guaranteed wish won't save them.
Cue story of the player whose last move resulted in "For what do you
wish?", then died before the resulting item could be used.

  If you let yourself get deep enough into trouble that a magic lamp
wish won't help, you're playing too carelessly.  Remember the lesson of
mrivan's ttyrecs:  Prepare for emergencies and there won't be any.
("The best way to get out of trouble in NetHack is not to get into it in
the first place."  I have found lit magic lamps to be a great way to
avoid getting into trouble in the first place.  It's tough to avoid what
you don't know about.)

>I would not be surprised if telling an
