  I would be surprised.  Assuming "immediately upped their statistics
significantly" means significant AC and armor weight improvement. 

  Minetown is the worst place to use a wish on DSM.  No other place in
the entire dungeon makes lightweight AC easier to get.  
  - A priest to buy protection from. 
    - weightless AC 
  - Shops to get money for protection from.  
    - Pets can help here.
  - Major armor source in the Minetown Watch.  
    - Pets can help here as well.
    - Armor enchantment is weightless.
  - Altar to easily and authoritatively buc armor.  
    - From, say, the Minetown Watch.
    - Also from levels immediately above/below.
  - Good chance of mithril armor in the Gnomish Mines.
    - 6 AC vs 9 of DSM
    - Weight 150 vs 40
      - Remember, it's the AC increase vs weight of all armor 
        combined that needs to be significantly improved.

  Wishing for DSM in MineTown is like wishing for a luckstone in
MinesEnd.

  DSM at +1 (average enchantments result) gives 10 points of AC.  +0
Elven mithril gives 5.  +0 Dwarven mithril 6.  The percentage
improvement in AC and weight for DSM isn't that great.  Especially when
you consider the 4 other pieces of armor the player should be wearing.
Even more so when you consider the weightless AC the player can get from
divine protection and armor enchantments.

  Add in found enchantments and DSM doesn't look significant in terms of
armor.  (I generally have +4 total in found enchantments by the time I
reach MineTown.  Easily.)

  

  An unexperienced player is also much less likely to successfully wish
for armor.  Even if the genie grants a wish.  They're also less likely
to make good use of it if the wish does succeed.  (No, I'm not assuming
failure.  I'm just not assuming a granted wish will automatically
succeed.  Because they don't.  As I know from bitter experience.)  

  In fact, successful wishes seem more like delayed instadeaths for
unexperienced players.  Sloppy play results.  The most you can hope
they'll learn from the experience is not to do that again.  They could
have just been told that in the first place.

  Unlike the AC gaining methods listed above, the failure mode for
wasting a magic lamp has bad short-term and long term effects.  Even
medium term as a magic lamp is great for exploring below MineTown down
to Mines End.  Yet another reason MineTown is the worst place to try to
use a Magic Lamp for a wish for DSM.



